From 3a1fe757cad16ad7db9e6334d9013d216adc31da Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jolyon Brown <jolyon@limilo.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 08:39:40 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 37/40] Count stores through a pointer as global stores of a
 function

NativeCodeBasicBlock::CheckGlobalAliasing decides whether a function is
flagged LOBJF_NO_GLOBAL_STORES. It looked at calls and at stores in the
absolute, absolute indexed and indirect addressing modes, but not at
"STA (zp),y" or "STA (zp,x)", so a function whose only store goes
through a pointer parameter was flagged as storing to no global.

The flag has one reader: CheckSingleUseGlobalLoad, which lets the
peephole optimiser replace reads of a zero page register by reads of the
global the register was loaded from, and walks past a JSR to a flagged
function. With

	char x = g;
	bump(&g);		// void bump(char * p) { p[0] += 100; }
	return x;

the copy of g that was taken before the call was dropped and g read
again behind it, in native code at every optimisation level. The same
for struct members changed through a struct pointer, for elements of
local arrays with a fixed address, for zero page globals, for a callee
that passes the pointer on or takes it from a global, and for the
library's memset and strcpy.

Stores in the two indirect indexed modes now count. This also covers
stores into the function's own stack frame, which cannot hit a global;
the flag is lost for such functions, which only costs forwarding.

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 oscar64/NativeCodeGenerator.cpp | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/oscar64/NativeCodeGenerator.cpp b/oscar64/NativeCodeGenerator.cpp
index 7b070bb..13d18c6 100644
--- a/oscar64/NativeCodeGenerator.cpp
+++ b/oscar64/NativeCodeGenerator.cpp
@@ -17205,8 +17205,11 @@ void NativeCodeBasicBlock::CheckGlobalAliasing(bool& globalStores, bool& globalL
 					globalStores = true;
 				}
 			}
-			else if (ins.mMode == ASMIM_ABSOLUTE || ins.mMode == ASMIM_ABSOLUTE_X || ins.mMode == ASMIM_ABSOLUTE_Y || ins.mMode == ASMIM_INDIRECT)
+			else if (ins.mMode == ASMIM_ABSOLUTE || ins.mMode == ASMIM_ABSOLUTE_X || ins.mMode == ASMIM_ABSOLUTE_Y || ins.mMode == ASMIM_INDIRECT ||
+				ins.mMode == ASMIM_INDIRECT_X || ins.mMode == ASMIM_INDIRECT_Y)
 			{
+				// A store through a pointer may hit any global: "STA (P0),y" in
+				// a function called with the address of one.
 				if (ins.mType == ASMIT_INC || ins.mType == ASMIT_DEC || ins.mType == ASMIT_ASL || ins.mType == ASMIT_LSR || ins.mType == ASMIT_ROL || ins.mType == ASMIT_ROR)
 				{
 					globalLoads = true;
